# Byte-exact fixtures: git must never translate line endings in these.
#
# This is not belt-and-braces. `core.autocrlf` defaults to TRUE on GitHub's
# windows-latest runners, and git decides text-vs-binary by scanning only the
# FIRST 8000 BYTES for a NUL. An encrypted content blob is high-entropy bytes
# with no guaranteed NUL — a 16-byte blob may well have none at all — so git is
# free to classify it as text and rewrite every 0x0A to 0x0D 0x0A on checkout.
#
# The blob would then decrypt to garbage on Windows and only on Windows, while
# the code is provably correct, and the failure would look like a decoder bug.
tests/data/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
